<title>USA: Navistar International Corp Q2 net up.</title>
<headline>Navistar International Corp Q2 net up.</headline>
<dateline>CHICAGO 1997-05-15</dateline>
<text>
<p>1997			1996</p>
<p> Shr			  $0.31		    $0.26</p>
<p> Net			 30,000		   26,000</p>
<p> Revs		   1,551,000		1,480,000</p>
<p> Avg shrs		  73,700		   73,800</p>
<p>	   6 MONTHS</p>
<p> Shr			  $0.41		    $0.46</p>
<p> Net			 45,000		   48,000</p>
<p> Revs		   2,847,000		2,912,000</p>
<p> Avg shrs		  73,700		   73,800</p>
<p>(All data above 000s except per share numbers)  </p>
<p>NOTE: '97 Q2 results includes a $109 million contribution to hourly and salaried pension plans. Navistar contributed $105 million to the plans in the first quarter.</p>
<p>The amounts were the regularly planned contributions scheduled to be made during fiscal years 1997 and 1998, Navistar said. The timing of the contributions allows for their deduction on Navistar's 1996 tax return, creating a tax loss in that year that can be carried forward 15 years. As a result, previously incurred tax losses that expire in 1998 will most likely be used.</p>
<p>((Chicago Newsdesk 312-408-8787))</p>
